
On the CBus there are two valve controls for the HVAC ducts - '1 AC V Bedrooms' and '1 AC V Main'.  The bedrooms are on the east and north
sides of the house and currently the north bedrooms are not used so the doors are usually closed.  The main vent services the west side
of the house, which also has some north windows, and it sends some air to the ground floor space that is well shaded and so direction
of the windows does not play a big part
in how well the HVAC works.  At least one of these valves must be open at all times, and change-over should open both and then close the one
we want to close.  During the day (e.g. after 0900) the bedrooms do not need heating/cooling and so they should be closed so that all the
HVAC effort goes into the main house area.  Once the sun goes down, the bedrooms can again be opened and processed.  If the house is still
heating/cooling after 2200 then the main valve can close to 50% to push more of the air to the bedrooms.  At present, closing the main
valve and leaving the bedrooms open tends to make a lot of air noise so we wont close it completely until I have researched the cause and
resolved.

